error[fixed_outside_a_group]: `i64[2][3]` is a C array member, so it stands only as a field of a `record` inside an `extern` group, whose layout a C compiler chose — here no group's record holds it (§4.19)
  at tests/golden/full/fixedbugs-405-a-nested-fixed-array-is-told-its-whole-type-growable.hero:15:8
     |
  15 |     x: i64[2][3] @ [[1, 2], [3, 4], [5, 6]]  #~ fixed_outside_a_group
     |        ^^^^^^^^^
  note: where no C struct holds it, use `[[i64]]`, built as `[a, b, c]` or grown with `push`: it grows, it is compared and hashed like any other value, and it is what every Heroes record holds

